        },
        "Vocations": {
            "name": "Vocations",
            "description": "<p>A deity may call upon their followers for more than just the traditional measures of their worship, but instead on a specific role the follower is meant to fill as their devotee, and you have heard this calling. This requires you to take on additional edicts and anathema that are adjoined with your vocation, and in exchange, you are afforded certain luxuries that other followers are not.</p>\n<p>Your vocation symbolizes your main mission as a cleric, so you can only have one vocation. Some deities may not have vocations of a certain kind or actively discourage certain vocations (such as a heretic for Torag who forbids lies or clinician for Zon-Kuthon). Other servitor’s of your deity may consider your methods unorthodox despite following their deity given your differences from the standard followers of the faith, and as such may not be helpful towards you despite sharing the same deity.</p>"
        }
    }
}
